WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Start with API activity. Reporting shows traffic and errors for the selected environment. This video uses simulated demo data.

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Choose the reporting period. The selected time window applies to these analytics. Other reports have their own filters.

3
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Export the displayed analytics. Export analytics downloads the activity summary as JSON. Request volume is not product consumption.

4
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:21.000
Review Consumption. Owners can inspect historical product quantities, complexity tiers, unit rates and amounts.

5
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:29.000
Open a usage record. This charge links to the borrower and origination. It is not a payment receipt.

6
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Use the historical rate. Compare quantity, complexity, unit rate and rate version. Do not apply today's prices to older charges.

7
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:41.000
Check Workload separately. Processed counts and agreed limits describe operations. They are separate from financial charges.

8
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:47.000
Open Reports & exports. Choose a completed export and inspect its format, source, part count and expiry.

9
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:52.000
Distinguish the file from its metadata. Download artifact retrieves the generated report. Export record JSON saves its descriptive record.

10
00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:58.000
Download the generated artifact. This example downloads a fictional risk package. For multipart exports, retrieve every part.

11
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:04.000
Save metadata when you need the trace. Keep the report ID and source reference. Request a new export if its download has expired.
